{"id":"lake-retba","name":"Lake Retba","qid":"Q1522557","country":"Senegal","locality":"Tivaouane Peulh-Niaga","lat":"14.838888888","lon":"-17.234444444","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Date not recorded","period":"","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"Tentative World Heritage Site; monument historique in Senegal","type":"salt lake; quarry","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Retba","text":"Lake Retba, also known as Lac Rose (meaning \"pink lake\"), lies north of the Cape Verde peninsula in Senegal, some 35 km (22 mi) north-east of the capital, Dakar. It is named for its pink waters caused by Dunaliella salina algae and is known for its high salt content, up to 40% in some areas. Its colour is usually particularly strong from late January to early March, during the dry season.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Retba","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-5219a1029996","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"Lac Rose in Senegal.jpg","o":"gh-5219a1029996.jpg","credit":{"text":"Arnault","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lac_Rose_in_Senegal.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-7a4898aaad83","w":1200,"h":677,"title":"Ngeej bu Retba.jpg","o":"gh-7a4898aaad83.jpg","credit":{"text":"DebyDB93","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ngeej_bu_Retba.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-a558c3463771","w":800,"h":1200,"title":"RetbaLake.png","o":"gh-a558c3463771.png","credit":{"text":"Jjm2311","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RetbaLake.png","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"civilization-vi--lake-retba","game":"civilization-vi","name":"Lake Retba","verified":false,"text":"","text_source":"","text_l